.TH LOGINS 1 
.SH NAME
logins   \- enable user logins
.br
nologins \- disable user logins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logins
.br
.B nologins
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I logins
and
.I nologins
commands allow the super-user
to selectively enable and disable user
logins.
The super-user may login as `root'
on any terminal even when logins are disabled.
.SH FILES
/etc/loglock	disables user logins
.br
/etc/sdloglock	system shutdown in progress
.SH "SEE ALSO"
login(1), shutdown(8)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
`No Logins',
a user attempted to login while logins
were disabled.
.br

`LOGINS DISABLED',
printed when the super-user logs in and
user logins are disabled.
